\n\nSubmit the presentation PPTX and one document containing your individual defence, reflection and AI-use declaration together. Include the repository URL and team ID where applicable. The marks assess submitted evidence: presentation 35, individual defence 40, reflection 20, declaration 5.\n\n## How to hand in\n\nOpen the correct cohort/assessment form below and read its current deadline. Fill the required identity fields; leave Team ID blank for individual work. Choose Add file > Upload and select the complete required file set. Wait for the filenames to appear, then click Submit. Keep the confirmation page and local copies. Each file must be at most 10 MB. If replacing work before the deadline, send the complete set again; the latest on-time response replaces the earlier response. If the form is closed or upload fails, keep your files and contact the lecturer; do not use a different assignment form.\n\nStudent submission link: https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLScnSPyvzCLfoHhIBusvFTIpqC-zAsk2bCLMqu6kJCh5cGI9gQ/viewform\n\nPublished closing time (UTC+03:00 is Kampala): 2026-12-18T14:00:00+03:00. Read the live form for any announced revision.\n\nPreparation guidance only until the lecturer releases this assessment after its grading checks. These instructions do not open a form or release an unvalidated assessment.\n"},{"key":"DA|S05","track":"DA","cohort":"DA","id":"S05","label":"S05","week":2,"title":"SQL analysis","maximum":100,"component":"DA","weight":15,"formats":["sql"],"opens_at":null,"closes_at":null,"preserve_existing":false,"grading":"sql","brief":"# DA S05 — SQL analysis\n\n## Start here\n\nUse your own DA learner ID from your roster. Sign in to upload with the Google account registered with the lecturer. If you need account or file help, read STUDENT_HOW_TO.md supplied with the student materials. A repository is a folder of saved project files; an upload form is where you hand in assessed work. Saving to a repository does not submit an assignment.\n\n## Do the work\n\n1. Install DB Browser for SQLite from https://sqlitebrowser.org/dl/ using the Windows or macOS installer for your computer, or use the prepared lab installation. It is a desktop application, not a website account; no database account is needed.\n2. Copy the supplied riverside.db into your session folder, open DB Browser, choose Open Database and select that copy. Choose Execute SQL. Follow the SQL lab examples before building the assessed query.\n3. Build the 2025 Delivered report, net of returns, with one row per rep/month. Return columns in this order: region, rep_name, month, gross_ugx, returned_ugx, net_ugx. Use rep region, retain walk-in orders and combine multiple return events before joining.\n4. Run your query using the Execute button. Check there are no duplicate rep/month keys, all months are in 2025, and net equals gross minus returns. Add a SQL comment identifying a rep to discuss and why; the discussion is formative.\n5. Save the SQL text from the Execute SQL editor as your learner ID followed by _S05.sql. If using a text editor, save plain text with a .sql extension, not .sql.txt. Reopen the file and execute it against the issued database.\n\n## Check and submit\n\nSubmit exactly ONE .sql file containing the final report query, optionally with comments beginning --. Do not submit the database, CSV result, screenshot or the entire lab exercise. Marks: row keys 25, gross 25, returns 25, net 25; amount tolerance is 1 UGX after rounding.\n\n## How to hand in\n\nOpen the correct cohort/assessment form below and read its current deadline. Fill the required identity fields; leave Team ID blank for individual work. Choose Add file > Upload and select the complete required file set. Wait for the filenames to appear, then click Submit. Keep the confirmation page and local copies. Each file must be at most 10 MB. If replacing work before the deadline, send the complete set again; the latest on-time response replaces the earlier response. I